Z||000005||Raydar||08-11-2001||09:44 AM||||Hugh, happy to help.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><A HREF="http://www.aaarims.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aaarims.com/</A>  If you ever see wheels that you like on a particular car, find 'em here. They give the size and bolt circle.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Word of warning for the above link...<BR>Check the hub size as well.<BR>The new Toyota Celica wheels are 17X7 and 5X100 bolt pattern. They WON'T fit on a Fiero. <BR>A guy posted on the "alt.autos.fiero" newsgroup a few weeks ago, and he was PISSED!!!<BR>Bought 'em off E-Bay, but the seller probably didn't know either.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||4
